Seam: Text::Nunjucks::Lib->js_array_sort($arr, $comparefn). It sorts in place and returns $arr; $comparefn undef means the default comparator. It ports third_party/v8/builtins/array-sort.tq at V8 tag 13.6.233.17 in .tq order (SortState as a hash): run detection, binary insertion, minimum run length, merge_collapse with the deeper invariant, merge_lo/merge_hi with gallops and min_gallop adaptation. Spec prelude: the TypeError comes first, even on an empty array, with V8's NoSideEffectsToString text (new Runtime _js_no_side_effects_to_string); undefined values are counted out, never compared, and written last; the default comparator is ToString plus js_string_compare; a user comparator's result goes through ToNumber, NaN counts as +0, -0 is not below 0; exceptions propagate as is; the receiver is written index by index at the end. Left out, each with a reason in the header comment: elements-kind accessors, holes (ADR 0001), the Smi fast path, the Smi clamps and overflow guards.

